      "text_raw": "The specifications of this\namplifier clearly show the\nconstant-bandwidth\nbehavior.\nFor example, for a R =\nF\n100 kV. The bandwidth is\njust over 200 kHz. It does\nnot depend on the actual\ngain.\nCurves are also given for\nR =10 kV and 1 kV. It is\nF\nclear that for the latter, a\ngain of 100 is not easily\nobtained. Indeed, for this\nvalue of R , a gain of 100\nF\nwould necessitate a R of a\nS\nmere 10 V!\nIn this case, the input resistance of the amplifier takes over. The curve bends to the left.\nAt a gain of 100, a bandwidth of 4 MHz results, which would require a GBW of 400 MHz if\nit were a voltage amplifier.",
